---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Security check for AI-built apps (Lovable, Replit, Claude Code) | Umut Çakır"
  description="Is your AI-built app safe to launch? A fixed-price security and go-live check for apps built with Lovable, Bolt, Replit or Claude Code. Plain-English report in 3 business days."
>
<main>
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="c grid">
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Security &amp; go-live checks for apps built with Lovable, Replit, Claude Code &amp; friends</p>
        <h1>Is your AI‑built app <span class="mark">safe to launch?</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">I check it like a home inspection — every room, in plain English. Before customers trust it with their data and their money, you’ll know exactly what to fix first.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn" href="/go-live-check">Book a Go-Live Check — $490 <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4"/></svg></a>
          <a class="tlink" href="#sample">See a sample report</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="facts"><li>Fixed price</li><li>Report in 3 business days</li><li>No calls needed</li></ul>
      </div>

      <div class="art">
        <!-- Cutaway "app house": each numbered pin is one of the six checks -->
        <svg class="house" viewBox="0 0 600 600" role="img" aria-label="Drawing of an app as a house, with six inspection points marked.">
          <g fill="none" stroke="#1B1915" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" filter="url(#hand)">
            <!-- ground -->
            <path d="M14 420H586" stroke-width="2"/>
            <path d="M40 420v110h520V420" fill="#F0EFEA"/>
            <!-- house body & roof -->
            <path d="M70 420V200h460v220" fill="#fff"/>
            <path d="M48 214L300 48l252 166" fill="#FFD84A"/>
            <path d="M408 120V72h40v74" fill="#fff"/>
            <!-- floors -->
            <path d="M70 310h460"/><path d="M300 200v220"/><path d="M300 420v110" stroke-dasharray="6 7"/>
            <!-- 01 doormat + key (ground floor left) -->
            <path d="M120 420V336h70v84" fill="#fff"/><circle cx="178" cy="380" r="3" fill="#1B1915"/>
            <path d="M98 420h112l-7 -11H105z" fill="#FFD84A"/>
            <path d="M203 417h12"/><circle cx="220" cy="417" r="4.5" fill="#fff"/>
            <!-- 02 back door ajar (ground floor right, side wall) -->
            <path d="M530 420V338"/><path d="M530 338l34 -10v92l-34 0" fill="#fff"/><path d="M552 378h4"/>
            <rect x="372" y="346" width="88" height="56" rx="4" fill="#fff"/><path d="M384 362h44M384 376h60M384 390h30"/>
            <!-- 03 open window, papers flying out (upper floor left) -->
            <rect x="110" y="232" width="110" height="58" fill="#fff"/><path d="M110 254h110"/><path d="M110 232l-26 -18h110l26 18" fill="#fff"/>
            <path d="M58 196l-14 -10 6 -14 16 8z" fill="#fff"/><path d="M28 238l-12 2 2 -14 12 2z" fill="#fff"/><path d="M76 168l-8 -12 12 -6 6 12z" fill="#fff"/>
            <!-- filing cabinet with open drawer -->
            <rect x="236" y="246" width="44" height="64" fill="#fff"/><path d="M236 268h44M236 288h44"/><path d="M232 272h52v-8" />
            <!-- 04 safe (upper floor right) -->
            <rect x="420" y="236" width="70" height="66" rx="4" fill="#fff"/><circle cx="455" cy="269" r="14"/><path d="M455 259v4M455 279v-4M445 269h4M465 269h-4"/>
            <!-- 06 smoke alarm on ceiling (upper floor right) -->
            <path d="M336 200v10"/><ellipse cx="336" cy="216" rx="18" ry="6" fill="#fff"/><path d="M330 228l-4 8M342 228l4 8" stroke-dasharray="2 5"/>
            <!-- 05 basement boxes -->
            <path d="M330 470h70v50h-70z" fill="#fff"/><path d="M330 470l10-14h70l-10 14"/><path d="M400 470l10-14v50l-10 14"/>
            <path d="M420 486h60v34h-60z" fill="#fff"/><path d="M352 494h26"/>
            <path d="M90 520v-56h120v56" fill="#fff"/><path d="M90 480h120"/>
          </g>
          <!-- inspector's red-pen pins -->
          <g font-family="Schibsted Grotesk, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">
            <g class="pin"><circle cx="246" cy="392" r="15" fill="#fff" stroke="#D23B1E" stroke-width="2"/><text x="246" y="397" fill="#D23B1E">1</text></g>
            <g class="pin"><circle cx="572" cy="314" r="15" fill="#fff" stroke="#D23B1E" stroke-width="2"/><text x="572" y="319" fill="#D23B1E">2</text></g>
            <g class="pin"><circle cx="36" cy="178" r="15" fill="#fff" stroke="#D23B1E" stroke-width="2"/><text x="36" y="183" fill="#D23B1E">3</text></g>
            <g class="pin"><circle cx="506" cy="236" r="15" fill="#fff" stroke="#D23B1E" stroke-width="2"/><text x="506" y="241" fill="#D23B1E">4</text></g>
            <g class="pin"><circle cx="438" cy="452" r="15" fill="#fff" stroke="#D23B1E" stroke-width="2"/><text x="438" y="457" fill="#D23B1E">5</text></g>
            <g class="pin"><circle cx="374" cy="216" r="15" fill="#fff" stroke="#D23B1E" stroke-width="2"/><text x="374" y="221" fill="#D23B1E">6</text></g>
          </g>
          <!-- handwritten note -->
          <g font-family="Schibsted Grotesk, system-ui, sans-serif" font-style="italic" font-size="17" fill="#D23B1E">
            <text x="60" y="584">keys under the mat!</text>
          </g>
          <path d="M218 578c34-4 30-60 6-150" fill="none" stroke="#D23B1E" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M216 440l8-12 6 14" fill="none" stroke="#D23B1E" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
        <ol class="legend"><li><b>1</b>Secret keys</li><li><b>2</b>Admin pages</li><li><b>3</b>Customer data</li><li><b>4</b>Payments</li><li><b>5</b>Backups</li><li><b>6</b>Error alerts</li></ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ticker" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="track">
      <span>Keys under the doormat<small>= secret keys in your code</small></span><span>Back door unlocked<small>= admin pages anyone can open</small></span><span>Files out the window<small>= customer data strangers can read</small></span><span>Nobody checked the safe<small>= payments that aren’t verified</small></span><span>Boxes never opened<small>= backups nobody tested</small></span><span>Smoke alarm, no batteries<small>= errors nobody hears about</small></span><span>Keys under the doormat<small>= secret keys in your code</small></span><span>Back door unlocked<small>= admin pages anyone can open</small></span><span>Files out the window<small>= customer data strangers can read</small></span><span>Nobody checked the safe<small>= payments that aren’t verified</small></span><span>Boxes never opened<small>= backups nobody tested</small></span><span>Smoke alarm, no batteries<small>= errors nobody hears about</small></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section id="checks">
    <div class="c grid">
      <div class="head reveal"><p class="eyebrow">What I check</p><h2>Six things that decide whether your app is <em>ready</em>.</h2><p class="lead">Each one is a real problem in apps built with Lovable, Bolt, Replit or Claude Code — usually running on Supabase or Firebase — explained in words that don’t need a developer to translate.</p></div>
      <div class="checks">
        <div class="check reveal"><div class="top"><span class="num">1</span>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" fill="none" stroke="#1B1915" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" filter="url(#hand)"><path d="M8 52h80l-8 14H16z" fill="#FFD84A"/><circle cx="62" cy="50" r="7" fill="#fff"/><path d="M55 50H30M38 50v6M44 50v4"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Secret keys left in your app</h3><p class="meta">“keys under the doormat”</p><p>API keys sitting in your app’s code, where anyone can copy them.</p><p class="means"><b>Means:</b> surprise bills, or a stranger in your data.</p></div>
        <div class="check reveal"><div class="top"><span class="num">2</span>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" fill="none" stroke="#1B1915" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" filter="url(#hand)"><path d="M24 66V8h40v58"/><path d="M24 8l30 8v56l-30-6z" fill="#fff"/><path d="M46 40h3"/><path d="M70 30l12-6M70 40h14M70 50l12 6" stroke="#D23B1E"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Admin pages anyone can open</h3><p class="meta">“the back door is unlocked”</p><p>Admin pages that open without logging in.</p><p class="means"><b>Means:</b> anyone can change your prices, bookings or users.</p></div>
        <div class="check reveal"><div class="top"><span class="num">3</span>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" fill="none" stroke="#1B1915" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" filter="url(#hand)"><rect x="34" y="26" width="52" height="40" fill="#fff"/><path d="M34 42h52"/><path d="M22 18l-10-6 4-10 12 6z" fill="#fff"/><path d="M14 40l-10 2 2-12 10 2z" fill="#fff"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Customer data strangers can read</h3><p class="meta">“files out the window”</p><p>One customer can see another customer’s details — or a stranger can see everyone’s.</p><p class="means"><b>Means:</b> a data leak, and the trust that goes with it.</p></div>
        <div class="check reveal"><div class="top"><span class="num">4</span>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" fill="none" stroke="#1B1915" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" filter="url(#hand)"><rect x="22" y="8" width="56" height="56" rx="4" fill="#fff"/><circle cx="50" cy="36" r="12"/><path d="M50 26v4M50 46v-4M40 36h4M60 36h-4"/><path d="M28 64v6M72 64v6"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Payments that aren’t verified</h3><p class="meta">“nobody checked the safe”</p><p>Payments that look fine but aren’t verified, and refunds nobody tested.</p><p class="means"><b>Means:</b> customers marked “paid” who never paid.</p></div>
        <div class="check reveal"><div class="top"><span class="num">5</span>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" fill="none" stroke="#1B1915" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" filter="url(#hand)"><path d="M14 30h44v36H14z" fill="#fff"/><path d="M14 30l8-10h44l-8 10M58 30l8-10v36l-8 10"/><path d="M26 44h20"/><path d="M62 52h22v14H62z" fill="#FFD84A"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Backups nobody has tested</h3><p class="meta">“boxes in the basement”</p><p>Backups that exist, but have never been restored even once.</p><p class="means"><b>Means:</b> one bad click and the data is gone for good.</p></div>
        <div class="check reveal"><div class="top"><span class="num">6</span>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" fill="none" stroke="#1B1915" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" filter="url(#hand)"><path d="M48 4v10"/><ellipse cx="48" cy="22" rx="26" ry="8" fill="#fff"/><path d="M40 38l-6 12M56 38l6 12M48 40v14" stroke-dasharray="2 6"/><path d="M70 50l14 14M84 50L70 64" stroke="#D23B1E"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Errors nobody hears about</h3><p class="meta">“smoke alarm, no batteries”</p><p>Errors happen silently, and you only hear about them from customers.</p><p class="means"><b>Means:</b> problems that grow for weeks before anyone notices.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="more reveal"><a class="tlink" href="/go-live-check#checklist">See the full checklist</a> →</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="stage" id="sample">
    <div class="c grid">
      <div class="intro reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">The report</p>
        <h2>What you get, in plain English.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Every finding says what’s wrong, why it matters to your business, and how urgent it is. Plus a 10-minute video walking you through it.</p>
      </div>
      <article class="report reveal" aria-label="Sample report">
        <div class="rhead">
          <div><small>Sample report · Booking app for a cleaning company</small><h3>Go-Live Report</h3></div>
          <span class="seal">Inspected by Umut</span>
        </div>
        <div class="tally">
          <div><b class="t-r">3</b><span>Fix now</span></div>
          <div><b class="t-a">5</b><span>Fix soon</span></div>
          <div><b class="t-g">12</b><span>Looks good</span></div>
        </div>
        <ul class="items">
          <li><span class="pill p-r">Fix now</span><div><strong>Anyone with the link can read every customer’s name and address.</strong><p>Data access rules are switched off on the customers table.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pill p-r">Fix now</span><div><strong>The admin page opens without logging in.</strong><p>One missing check on the /admin route.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pill p-r">Fix now</span><div><strong>A customer could mark their own booking as paid.</strong><p>Payment confirmations aren’t verified.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pill p-a">Fix soon</span><div><strong>Backups exist, but nobody has ever tried restoring one.</strong></div></li>
          <li><span class="pill p-g">Looks good</span><div><strong>Passwords are handled properly by your login provider.</strong></div></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="rfoot"><span><b>Inspector’s note:</b> start with the three red items — about two days of work.</span><a class="tlink" href="/go-live-check#sample">What’s in a full report</a></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="c grid">
      <div class="head reveal"><p class="eyebrow">How it works</p><h2>Three steps. <em>No calls.</em></h2></div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step reveal"><div class="dot">1</div><span class="k">Day 0</span><h3>Invite me</h3><p>Add me as a collaborator to your project. No passwords, and you can remove me anytime.</p></div>
        <div class="step reveal"><div class="dot">2</div><span class="k">Days 1–3</span><h3>I inspect every room</h3><p>I test your app the way a curious stranger would, then check the code behind it.</p></div>
        <div class="step reveal"><div class="dot">3</div><span class="k">Day 3</span><h3>You get the answer</h3><p>A plain-English report and a short video. Fix it yourself, or let me do it.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="dark" id="pricing">
    <div class="c grid">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p><h2>One fixed price. No hourly surprises.</h2></div>
      <div class="plans">
        <div class="plan"><span class="tag"></span><h3>Go-Live Check</h3><div class="price">$490</div><div class="when">Report in 3 business days</div>
          <ul><li>All six checks</li><li>Plain-English report, ranked by urgency</li><li>10-minute video walkthrough</li><li>One app, up to ~20 screens</li></ul>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/go-live-check#start">Start a check</a></div>
        <div class="plan best"><span class="tag">Recommended</span><h3>Check + Fix</h3><div class="price">$1,490</div><div class="when">Done in 5–7 business days</div>
          <ul><li>Everything in the Go-Live Check</li><li>I fix every critical and serious issue</li><li>Re-tested, with before/after proof</li><li>Backups and error alerts set up</li></ul>
          <a class="btn y" href="/go-live-check#start">Check and fix my app</a></div>
        <div class="plan"><span class="tag"></span><h3>Care Plan</h3><div class="price">$290<small> / month</small></div><div class="when">Cancel anytime</div>
          <ul><li>Monthly security check</li><li>Updates and backup tests</li><li>Up to 2 hours of small changes</li><li>Reply within 48 hours</li></ul>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/go-live-check#start">Keep my app healthy</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="promise">
        <p><b>Your $490 counts toward a fix.</b>Upgrade to Check + Fix within 14 days and the check is credited in full.</p>
        <p><b>Nothing serious? You don’t pay.</b>If I can’t find a single serious issue, the check is free.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section id="about">
    <div class="c grid about">
      <div class="ph reveal">Photo<span class="tagnote">Umut, your inspector</span></div>
      <div class="tx reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Who you’d be working with</p>
        <h2>You talk to the person doing the work.</h2>
        <p>I’ve built software for nine years. For the last four, I’ve worked on the desktop app of an end-to-end encrypted messaging product — the kind where a small security mistake is never small.</p>
        <p>I use AI tools every day, so I know where they shine and where they quietly cut corners. No sales team, no juniors. Just me, and a careful look at your app.</p>
        <div class="sig">
          <svg width="150" height="44" viewBox="0 0 150 44" fill="none" stroke="#1B1915" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" filter="url(#hand)"><path d="M6 30c4-16 9-20 10-8s5 12 9-2 6-8 7 2 5 6 9-8c4-8 7 2 10 6s8-12 13-10 4 12 10 7 9-12 15-5 11 4 17-3 14 3 22-3"/><path d="M8 38c40 2 90-1 130-4" stroke-width="1.4"/></svg>
          <span><b style="font-weight:600">Umut Çakır</b><small>Software engineer · Istanbul</small></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="c grid">
      <div class="faq reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
        <h2 style="margin-bottom:40px">Fair questions.</h2>
        <details open><summary>Do I need to give you my passwords?<i></i></summary><p>No. You invite me as a collaborator (for example in Lovable, GitHub or Supabase), and remove me the moment we’re done.</p></details>
        <details><summary>I’m not technical. Will I understand the report?<i></i></summary><p>That’s the point of it. Every issue says what’s wrong, why it matters to your business, and how urgent it is — in plain words.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Which tools do you work with?<i></i></summary><p>Apps built with Lovable, Bolt, Replit, Claude Code or Cursor, running on Supabase or Firebase. For Bubble and Base44 I can inspect and report; fixes are limited.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is my Lovable (or Bolt, Replit) app secure by default?<i></i></summary><p>Not always. The most common problem is that the database’s access rules (Supabase “RLS”) are missing or too open, so one customer — or a stranger — can read other people’s data. It’s quick to check and usually quick to fix.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What if you don’t find anything?<i></i></summary><p>Then you know your app is in good shape — and you don’t pay.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="end" style="background:var(--yellow);border-top:1.5px solid var(--ink)">
    <div class="c">
      <h2 class="reveal">Check the locks<br>before you open<br>the doors.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Fixed price, plain English, three business days.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/go-live-check">Book a Go-Live Check — $490 <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
</Base>
<style>
  .more{grid-column:1 / -1;margin-top:28px;font-size:18px}
</style>
